msgid "Arbitrary customizations"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus allows users to arbitrarily customize the options of HTTP servers "
"started by Quarkus via the use of `io.quarkus.vertx.http."
"HttpServerOptionsCustomizer`.\n"
"For example, if the HTTP port needs to be set programmatically, then the "
"following code could be used:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"By making the class a managed bean, Quarkus will take the customizer into "
"account when it starts the Vert.x servers"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In this case, we only care about customizing the HTTP server, so we just "
"override the `customizeHttpServer` method, but users should be aware that "
"`HttpServerOptionsCustomizer` allows configuring the HTTPS and Domain Socket "
"servers as well"
msgstr ""

msgid "How to execute logic when HTTP server started"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In order to execute some custom action when the HTTP server is started "
"you'll need to declare an _asynchronous_ CDI observer method.\n"
"Quarkus _asynchronously_ fires CDI events of types `io.quarkus.vertx.http."
"HttpServerStart`, `io.quarkus.vertx.http.HttpsServerStart` and `io.quarkus."
"vertx.http.DomainSocketServerStart` when the corresponding HTTP server "
"starts listening on the configured host and port."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"An asynchronous `HttpServerStart` observer method may be declared by "
"annotating an `HttpServerStart` parameter with `@jakarta.enterprise.event."
"ObservesAsync`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Running behind a reverse proxy"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus could be accessed through proxies that additionally generate headers "
"(e.g. `X-Forwarded-Host`) to keep\n"
"information from the client-facing side of the proxy servers that is altered "
"or lost when they are involved.\n"
"In those scenarios, Quarkus can be configured to automatically update "
"information like protocol, host, port and URI\n"
